// The parameters of `main` are the inputs of a run (design principles 3.9/9.3): a program whose
// entry has an open parameter cannot be executed, and the driver says so before any scheduling pass
// that executes. `std::nop` is not one of those -- it ends the pipeline without a run -- so a
// pipeline that ends in it must not ask for `x`. The plan beside this file pins both directions:
// `std::nop` alone is quiet, `std::nvm` reports the missing argument.
func main(x: int) => int sync {
    println(x)
    return x
}